    LineComment "// Index access reads and writes a collection by subscript. A read coll[i]"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// desugars to coll.get(i), a write coll[i] = v to coll = coll.set(i, v) — the"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// same desugaring-to-a-method strategy operators use (1 + 2 is 1.add(2)). No"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// new value form reaches the type checker or the folder: a subscript is a call."
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "//"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// A read can miss — an index out of range, a key not present — so it yields a"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// result union (V | error), the same shape a fallible function returns. A write"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// returns the new collection (self): data stays immutable, and the let local is"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// rebound to it. A map write is an upsert and always succeeds; a list write past"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// the end is a bug caught at compile time (index_out_of_range), not a value."
    Newline "\n"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// Reading a list element. The static type is int | error — the read may be out"
    Newline "\n"
    LineComment "// of range — even when the index is a constant the folder can resolve."
    Newline "\n"
